WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:03.169
AstroWeb brings your night sky photographs to
life.

00:04.140 --> 00:09.537
From AstroWizard, export the final image, the
starless background, and both star layers.

00:10.140 --> 00:13.703
In Studio, place zoom frames over the details
you want to visit.

00:15.140 --> 00:18.447
Separate layers let the stars drift across the
glowing gas.

00:19.140 --> 00:24.618
A sky journey starts with the whole Milky Way,
then follows the sky coordinates to your
photograph.

00:27.140 --> 00:33.305
Here in Andromeda, dust lanes line up as your
own image dissolves into a much deeper Hubble
mosaic.

00:36.140 --> 00:40.426
Closer to home, spacecraft images reveal flares,
craters, and storms.

00:41.140 --> 00:44.468
The polar chart puts your photograph among the
constellations.

00:45.140 --> 00:47.828
Seen from above, the nebula lies near our Sun.

00:49.140 --> 00:51.277
Find your photo in the night panorama.

00:52.140 --> 00:58.156
On Google TV, browse with the remote. Open a
film, choose a destination, or zoom into a map.

01:02.140 --> 01:06.279
Your server and TV can share the collection on a
private home network.
